<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Android 12 (API 31) replaced the windowBackground splash with a system
      splash: an icon, centred, on a solid colour. It does not read
      launch_background, so without the attributes below it picks its own
      colour â€” white in light mode, and in dark mode black, which would be a
      black flash in front of a light video.

      windowSplashScreenBackground is the top stop of the video's gradient: the
      same value the launch window was already using, so the system splash and
      the window behind Flutter are the same colour and the changeover is not
      visible.

      windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon is set to a deliberately BLANK drawable
      (res/drawable/splash_icon.xml). Left alone, it defaults to the app's
      launcher icon, which drew the shop's mark here motionless and then had the
      launch video animate the same mark a moment later â€” the same drawing
      twice, once dead, which reads as a stutter rather than a title. The
      video's opening frame contains no logo (the mark springs in at about
      1.25 s), so the backdrop alone is the frame that actually continues into
      the film.

      Only LaunchTheme is restated here. Resource qualifying is per-style, so
      this file replaces LaunchTheme for API 31+ while NormalTheme still
      resolves from values/ â€” or from values-night/ in dark mode, because night
      mode outranks platform version in Android's resource selection. That is
      exactly why values-night-v31/styles.xml exists as well.
    -->
    <style name="LaunchTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Light.NoTitleBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/launch_background</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">true</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splash_top</item>
        <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon</item>
    </style>
</resources>
